import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Plan 0014 — Certified re-expression: from proofs to delivery","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/plans/0014-certified-re-expression.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/plans/0014-certified-re-expression.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/plans/0014-certified-re-expression.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="plan-0014-—-certified-re-expression-from-proofs-to-delivery" tabindex="-1">Plan 0014 — Certified re-expression: from proofs to delivery <a class="header-anchor" href="#plan-0014-—-certified-re-expression-from-proofs-to-delivery" aria-label="Permalink to “Plan 0014 — Certified re-expression: from proofs to delivery”">​</a></h1><p>Status: draft. Depends on 0006/0007/0008/0009 (done), 0011 (morphism engine, landed), 0012 (bounded, landed), ADR 0002 (the thesis). Feeds 0013 (contraction search) as the discovery layer.</p><h2 id="goal" tabindex="-1">Goal <a class="header-anchor" href="#goal" aria-label="Permalink to “Goal”">​</a></h2><p>Convert the categorical reach the engine already proves into delivered performance and memory where structure exists. Today the project is theory-rich and conversion-poor: it <em>finds</em> the structures (carriers, scans, streaming softmax, KV sharing) but the carrier forms lose to Inductor&#39;s fused kernels (per-leaf dispatch).</p><p>The plan makes <strong>architecture the variable</strong> — search certified structural variants (head/KV sharing, expert tying, adapter merging, residual reassociation) and deliver the cheapest variant within a proven <code>error_budget</code>.</p><h2 id="delivery-—-two-paths" tabindex="-1">Delivery — two paths <a class="header-anchor" href="#delivery-—-two-paths" aria-label="Permalink to “Delivery — two paths”">​</a></h2><p>Delivery is not one problem; it splits by whether the extracted program expresses in Inductor&#39;s op set:</p><ul><li><strong>Standard forms</strong> (fold, reassociation, pairing, KV share, head collapse, tying) are ordinary matmul/add/etc. Hand Inductor the <em>better program</em> and it fuses and schedules it — <strong>the win lands, no gap to close.</strong> Extraction already routes here: <code>backend_cost(cost_fn, sink.supported_ops)</code> only prices forms the backend can lower.</li><li><strong>Carrier forms</strong> (scan, streaming softmax, batched levels) are outside Inductor&#39;s reach, so each leaf dispatches separately and the carrier loses. These need the fused executor (stage 1).</li></ul><p>Most architecture-level wins are the first kind; the fused executor is a carrier-only concern.</p><h2 id="mechanism-—-structural-interpretation" tabindex="-1">Mechanism — structural interpretation <a class="header-anchor" href="#mechanism-—-structural-interpretation" aria-label="Permalink to “Mechanism — structural interpretation”">​</a></h2><p>The model graph is <em>syntax</em> (ops = generators of the free monoidal category, wires = objects). A <strong>structural interpretation</strong> is a functor from that free category into a category of structures, and the structure supplies the laws: monoid → associativity (Blelloch), comonoid → <code>Δ</code> (pairing), traced → feedback (resolvents), hypergraph → contraction order. The interpretation adds no information — the function is fixed — it adds <strong>legality</strong>: which transformations are valid.</p><p>The interpretation is <strong>not unique</strong>. The same graph reads as plain composition (nothing to do), shared-input comonoid (pairing), low-rank (bounded), or a contraction problem — each exposing different rewrites. So <em>discovery = choosing the richest interpretation</em>, not applying laws inside a fixed one. That is what carrier recognition, the morphism engine, and 0013 do at successive levels.</p><p>Reach is the <strong>closure</strong> of the generators, not the generators themselves: the law library is the generating 2-cells, and the free higher category they generate <em>is</em> the reachable set. The e-graph already computes this higher structure (1-cells programs, 2-cells rewrites, 3-cells coherence via <code>_close_congruence</code>); budgets <strong>truncate</strong> it, and a truncation can miss but never mis-prove.</p><h2 id="stages" tabindex="-1">Stages <a class="header-anchor" href="#stages" aria-label="Permalink to “Stages”">​</a></h2><ol start="0"><li><p><strong>Real-block lifting</strong> (the gate). <code>_sig_liftable</code> declines multi-activation and mutated-cache blocks, so a real KV-cache attention block <code>(x, kv_cache)</code> never enters the search. Classify the cache as read-only state and lift multi-input attention blocks. Nothing downstream moves until this lands.</p></li><li><p><strong>Fused carrier executor</strong> (carrier-only). Measured carrier losses are per-leaf dispatch, not search. Fuse/tile <code>scan_lower</code> / <code>om_lower</code>, or capture decode into a CUDA graph, so a proven carrier converts to wall-time and memory instead of losing to Inductor&#39;s fused kernels. Standard-op wins need none of this — they ride Inductor (see Delivery).</p></li><li><p><strong>Certified variant search</strong> (architecture as the variable). Extend the morphism engine from match-and-apply to a search over structural variants, priced by a diagram-level cost model, each accepted only under a certificate (exact or within <code>error_budget</code>). Targets the bounded wins that already reproduce (tied-head collapse, 1.15–1.32×) and the named niche (decode KV, adapters, redundant heads).</p></li><li><p><strong>Structure zoo + production scale</strong> (the validation). A corpus of structured models (GQA, MoE, LoRA-merged, MLA-style KV, tied heads) and measurement at production dims (d≥1024, B≥8, real checkpoint, datacenter GPU). Required for any paper claim; the (now-retired) research writeup listed it as blocking.</p></li><li><p><strong>Contraction search (0013)</strong> — the discovery feeder. Replace the hand-written morphism laws with contraction-order search so sharing is <em>found</em>, not hand-coded. Sequenced <em>after</em> delivery works: discovering structure you cannot deliver is a proof, not a speedup.</p></li></ol><h2 id="bar" tabindex="-1">Bar <a class="header-anchor" href="#bar" aria-label="Permalink to “Bar”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Delivery:</strong> the fused carrier path beats Inductor on decode latency / peak memory in the structured regime — not raw prefill GEMM throughput.</li><li><strong>Conversion:</strong> a reified structural win converts to wall-time or memory at a rate that makes search worth its compile cost.</li><li><strong>Scale:</strong> ≥1.2× on a real checkpoint at production dims with certificates, or a documented reason why not.</li></ul><h2 id="risks" tabindex="-1">Risks <a class="header-anchor" href="#risks" aria-label="Permalink to “Risks”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Carrier delivery gap is a different discipline.</strong> Codegen/fusion for carriers is not categorical rewriting; closing it may need work outside the thesis. Standard-op wins ride Inductor and are unaffected — but a carrier win without a competitive executor is a proof, not a speedup.</li><li><strong>Structure is conditional.</strong> The census says stock dense models are thin; the wins live in structured models, so the zoo and the honest scope are load-bearing.</li><li><strong>Diagram cost model.</strong> Search is blind without a cost that ranks variants before reify; measure rank correlation (as <code>cost_fidelity.py</code> does) before trusting the search.</li><li><strong>Compile time.</strong> 262s at T=2048 vs Inductor&#39;s 45s — construction over saturation is also a compile-time lever.</li></ul><h2 id="non-goals" tabindex="-1">Non-goals <a class="header-anchor" href="#non-goals" aria-label="Permalink to “Non-goals”">​</a></h2><ul><li>Weight-space compression (ADR 0001).</li><li>Beating Inductor on raw prefill GEMM throughput.</li><li>Reinforcement learning. Directed search (bound + decompose + beam) handles the exponential joint move space — the Catalan bracketing search already does — because structure is what makes search beat RL.</li></ul><h2 id="see-also" tabindex="-1">See also <a class="header-anchor" href="#see-also" aria-label="Permalink to “See also”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>docs/mechanism.md</code> — the syntax → structure → match → rewrite loop this plan implements.</li><li><code>project/adrs/0002-categorical-re-expression-thesis.md</code> — the thesis and its mandatory consistency follow-ups.</li></ul>`,23)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};